course: dictionary
lesson: 15403
title: Sudden and unplanned
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spontaneously means doing something suddenly, without planning it first, because you feel like doing it. «Mia spontaneously grabbed her coat and ran out to the park.» Nobody had told her to go. She just did it.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Planned would mean she thought about it first, but grabbed and ran out happen quickly, with no list of steps. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Mia suddenly grabbed her coat and ran out to the park» still makes sense, so spontaneously means suddenly, without planning.
explain: In science, the meaning is a little different. Something happens spontaneously when it happens by itself, with nothing from outside causing it at that moment. The idea is the same: there is no outside push, and nobody set it up in advance.
fact: Spontaneously is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Spontaneous» is the adjective: a spontaneous picnic is one nobody planned.
fact: «The class spontaneously burst into song.» The singing began suddenly, because they felt like it.
fact: In science, a change that happens spontaneously happens by itself, with nothing from outside causing it at that moment.
fact: A spontaneous act of kindness is one nobody asked for.
exercise: «The crowd spontaneously started clapping.» What does spontaneously mean here? | Because the teacher told them to | After a long rehearsal | Very slowly, one clap at a time | *Suddenly, without planning
exercise: Which action was done spontaneously? | Jo sang a song she had practised for weeks | Jo wrote a list of songs to sing tomorrow | Jo read a song from a book | *Jo sang a song because the music started and she felt like it
exercise: In science, what does it mean if a change happens spontaneously? | *It happens by itself, with nothing from outside causing it at that moment | It happens because someone pushes it from outside | It happens only at night | It never happens at all
test: «We spontaneously went to the beach after lunch.» What does spontaneously suggest? | Sleepy and slow | Planned for weeks in a diary | Sad and grey | *Decided suddenly, without planning
test: Which example shows a spontaneous act of kindness? | Writing a rule about how to help people | *Carrying a stranger's bag up the stairs, though nobody asked | Waiting for a reward before helping | Helping a neighbour with shopping because they asked for help
exam: Ben says «spontaneously» means carefully planned in advance. What is the right meaning? | Done only on Sundays | Carefully planned in advance | *Suddenly, without planning first | Done slowly and with great care
